sky blue, with darker shades for group tasks and vibrant gradients for regular tasks. Internal text is displayed if the bar width is sufficient, while the task title and assignee are always shown adjacent to the bar to increase readability.\n\n\nAnalyzing data flow reveals that creating a task in one interface triggers database updates impacting all three views. Specifically, creating/editing in one view initiates a database write, followed by a refresh request. This refresh is expected to update data across the `tasks`, `ganttItems`, and `employees` datasets.\n\nFocusing on the database write, two sets of data will be created/updated: one for `ganttItems`, the other for `tasks`. The `ganttItems` update is designed to affect Gantt chart visuals directly, and task details update the \"Phân Công Công Việc\" view. The `employees` data is expected to be updated by counting tasks from both `db.tasks` and `db.ganttItems`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\GiaWyy\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\aps-project-manager\\\\backend\\\\src\\\\controllers\\\\projectController.js\"","EndLine":"303","StartLine":"240","toolAction":"\"Viewing projectController delete and move methods\"","toolSummary":"\"View projectController remaining code\""}}]}
